+# GriefLogger Yuuniverse changes
 
-Switched SQLite 3.47.2.0 from Shadow flattening to Loom include/Jar-in-Jar and marked version 1.2.10-1.21.1-yuuniverse.1. The official release fails Java module resolution when combined with Yuuniverse Economy's SQLite module. No gameplay/database Java code changed; the complete nested driver, native resources and JDBC service metadata remain present.
+## 2026-10-23T11:54:24.3154992+08:00 (UTC+08:00) - Retain queued SQL writes until confirmed commit
 
-Validation: :neoforge:build succeeds (no upstream tests in this source set). Archive inspection confirms no root org/sqlite classes and a selectable nested driver. The combined 65-JAR NeoForge 21.1.248 fixture starts and exits 0, initializes GriefLogger and Economy, and both SQLite databases pass read-only quick_check. Source baseline e913b78806a8f7646b7e3adc0d6721d1b386f29d. Production data, gameplay/MySQL and physical-client acceptance are outside this fixture.
+Based on 0017e15321badb496e4939c58ec7a60cf3821139 (the existing SQLite packaging patch on upstream e913b78806a8f7646b7e3adc0d6721d1b386f29d). Version 1.2.10-1.21.1-yuuniverse.2 preserves the upstream Apache-2.0 license and existing selectable SQLite packaging.
+
+A real transient SQLite lock discarded a queued observation in the preceding provider. Native repositories now queue owned SQL/parameter snapshots, including every batch row and copied binary values. Flushes retain their queue prefix until commit, serialize database writes and roll back failed attempts. Concurrent producers append safely. A known rollback permits complete replay with newly created JDBC statements. Ambiguous commit, failed rollback or unreconstructable legacy driver batches stop automatic flush with retained work and an explicit error. Post-commit cleanup cannot cause replay. Startup commits schema before event registration; ping closes its JDBC resources.
